# The scale check: 1000 nodes over 18 km - the town scenario's density, five times over - for an
# hour of traffic. CI's timing job runs it in a release build and fails if it takes longer than
# its budget: the simulator has to finish a 1000-node run in minutes for the comparison to be
# swept over seeds and parameters at all.
nodes     = 1000
placement = uniform
area      = 18000 x 18000

radio.sf     = 9
radio.bw     = 125000
radio.tx_dbm = 20

routing      = flood
routing.hops = 3
mac           = aloha
mac.max_delay = 2 s

traffic.interval  = 30 min
traffic.len       = 16..64
traffic.broadcast = 0.25

# Six hours to settle, the same for every candidate: on a quiet channel candidate 3's tables hold
# about 97% of routes by then, at every density the region is swept over, and under 12% after ten
# minutes. The traffic starts for the last three of them, so what is measured is a network already
# carrying it: candidate 3 decays under load, from 34% of unicasts on time in the first hour after a
# quiet warmup to under 10% from the third (MSH-50). Only the messages made after the warmup are
# counted, and only the airtime after it; the warmup's is reported apart.
warmup       = 6 h
traffic.lead = 3 h
duration     = 1 h
deadline     = 60 s
